.TITLE "say"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Converts text to audible speech using the system synthesizer. It can be used for accessibility, notifications, or simple fun in the terminal.

.DIV "TLDR"
**say "message"**
Speaks a specific string of text using the default system voice.
> __"message"__ the text to speak

**say -f file.txt**
Reads the contents of a text file aloud.
> __-f__ file input flag | __file.txt__ the source file

**say -v voice "message"**
Speaks the text using a specific voice name.
> __-v__ voice flag | __voice__ the name of the voice | __"message"__ text to speak

**say -o output.aiff "message"**
Saves the spoken text into an audio file instead of playing it.
> __-o__ output flag | __output.aiff__ the audio file name | __"message"__ text to record

.DIV "SUMMARY"
You can use the __say__ command at the end of a long-running script (e.g., `**./build.sh ; say "Finished"**`) to get an audible notification when the task is complete.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/say.html__
